    "description": "i3 Broadband builds and operates fiber-to-the-home broadband networks that provide internet, video, and voice services to residential and commercial customers. Its customer base is concentrated in regional U.S. markets where households and businesses require high-speed fixed connectivity, including central Illinois, the Chicago suburbs, greater St. Louis, southern Missouri, and Rhode Island. The operating model is asset heavy, with network construction, homes-passed expansion, and recurring subscription revenue forming the core business. Wren House states that the platform has more than 300,000 homes passed, while company materials trace the business back to a 1994 predecessor and document the later iTV-3 and i3 Broadband brands. Wren House acquired i3 Broadband in 2020, which it identifies as its first investment in the United States. Since that acquisition, the company has continued to expand its fiber footprint across existing and adjacent Midwestern markets.",
